        "aligned_char_end": 224,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 225,
        "char_start": 0,
        "effective_step": 1,
        "end_token_index": 76,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 77,
        "step_number": 1,
        "text": "Step 1: Calculate the vectors $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ given as $\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}$."
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 503,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 504,
        "char_start": 227,
        "effective_step": 2,
        "end_token_index": 182,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 183,
        "step_number": 2,
        "text": "Step 2: Find the vector $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ which is $\\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA}$. This gives us:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{AB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1230,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1231,
        "char_start": 506,
        "effective_step": 3,
        "end_token_index": 463,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 464,
        "step_number": 3,
        "text": "Step 3: Compute the cross product $\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{AB}$ to find a vector perpendicular to both $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AB}$, which will help in finding the area of the parallelogram formed by these two vectors. The cross product is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{AB} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -4 & -2 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i}(2 \\cdot -2 - 3 \\cdot -4) - \\mathbf{j}(1 \\cdot -2 - 3 \\cdot -4) + \\mathbf{k}(1 \\cdot -4 - 2 \\cdot -4)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i}(-4 + 12) - \\mathbf{j}(-2 + 12) + \\mathbf{k}(-4 + 8) = 8\\mathbf{i} - 10\\mathbf{j} + 4\\mathbf{k} = \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1470,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1471,
        "char_start": 1233,
        "effective_step": 4,
        "end_token_index": 561,
        "near_end": false,
        "prefix_token_count": 562,
        "step_number": 4,
        "text": "Step 4: Find the magnitude of the cross product vector $\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{AB}$:\n\\[\n\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{AB}\\| = \\sqrt{8^2 + (-10)^2 + 4^2} = \\sqrt{64 + 100 + 16} = \\sqrt{180} = 6\\sqrt{5}\n\\]"
      },
      {
        "aligned_char_end": 1841,
        "boundary_aligned_back": true,
        "char_end": 1842,
        "char_start": 1473,
        "effective_step": 5,
        "end_token_index": 681,
        "near_end": true,
        "prefix_token_count": 682,
        "step_number": 5,
        "text": "Step 5: The area of the parallelogram formed by vectors $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ is the magnitude of their cross product. Since the area of triangle $OAB$ is half the area of this parallelogram, we have:\n\\[\n\\text{Area of } \\triangle OAB = \\frac{1}{2} \\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{AB}\\| = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6\\sqrt{5} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]"
      }
    ]
