    "problem": "The points $O,$ $A,$ and $B$ satisfy $\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix}.$  Find the area of triangle $OAB.$",
    "solution": "The area of the parallelogram generated by $\\overrightarrow{OA}$ and $\\overrightarrow{OB}$ is given by\n\\[\\|\\overrightarrow{OA} \\times \\overrightarrow{OB}\\| = \\left\\| \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\end{pmatrix} \\times \\begin{pmatrix} -3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\end{pmatrix} \\right\\| = \\left\\| \\begin{pmatrix} 8 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} \\right\\| = 6 \\sqrt{5}.\\][asy]\nunitsize(0.4 cm);\n\npair A, B, C, D;\n\nA = (0,0);\nB = (7,2);\nC = (1,3);\nD = B + C;\n\ndraw(A--B,Arrow(6));\ndraw(A--C,Arrow(6));\ndraw(B--C);\ndraw(B--D--C,dashed);\n\nlabel(\"$O$\", A, SW);\nlabel(\"$A$\", B, SE);\nlabel(\"$B$\", C, W);\n[/asy]\n\nTherefore, the area of triangle $OAB$ is $\\boxed{3 \\sqrt{5}}.$",
